# The body of a generator that is walked in the loop or the spread that consumes it has a frame of its own, and that frame is the one of the body of a coroutine, which is shown wherever it stands. It was written into the image under the number of the function, which is the number of the unit that makes the generator: that one is shown only on top, so whoever asked for the caller got the file of the consumer, and a trace taken further up lacked the generator.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: a spread file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: for-of file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: a spread in a call file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: a default of a parameter file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: a generator in a generator file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: a finally file:///lib/helper.js
# CHECK-NEXT: below the top names < belowTop < consume
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
